  "name": "webapp2-auto",
  "description": "A Rust-based WebAssembly frontend for the Automatafl game, leveraging the Leptos framework to provide a reactive, client-side rendered user interface. It incorporates SVG-based board rendering, real-time game state updates via WebSockets, and a robust asynchronous API client for authentication and lobby management. The application follows a component-based architecture designed for high-performance browser execution with modular subsystems for chat, game views, and matchmaking.",
